pert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Missouri remains a Republican-leaning state in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly nine points toward the GOP. With the incumbent president term-limited, the 2028 race is open, removing any incumbency advantage for either side. No general-election polls or expert ratings are available yet, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying partisan balance.\n\nRepublican attention has centered on 2028 ambitions: Senator Josh Hawley has ruled out a White House bid, while Senator Eric Schmitt draws buzz as a potential vice-presidential pick. None of this changes the state's general-election lean. The Republican nominee starts with a clear advantage, and the race would likely require a substantial national shift or an unusually strong Democratic campaign to become competitive. Early activity is focused more on the parties' primaries than on the fall contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1545, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2074, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1871, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1883, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2013, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.183, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2061, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.204, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1925, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2006, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1989, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1976, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2056, "margin": -9.0}]}